SWEET IOMFB selectors (patch 0289, rule 7 sweep, user 2026-11-10): the AppleCLCD IOMobileFramebuffer user client answered every selector it did not implement with success + zeroed outputs. Selector map from IOMobileFramebuffer.framework _kern_* wrappers (research 133 section D). Now: SwapWait success (SwapEnd is synchronous); SetDebugFlags(15) -> previous flags 0; SetDisplayDevice(22) and EnableDisableVideoPowerSavings(33) accepted (one display, no power-saving mode); GetColorRemapMode(57) -> 0; GetDisplayArea(29) -> 62.39 x 135.10 mm as floats; GetMatrix(54) -> Q32.32 identity (zeros would make CA multiply by 0); GetDotPitch(28) -> float bits of 0.05546 mm (was the integer 458, which the framework reads as float bits); GetGammaTable(27), SupportedFrameInfo(74), SetBlock(78), GetBlock(79) and every other unknown selector -> kIOReturnUnsupported with a 'SWEET GAP: FB ... sel N' line (once per selector). No hardware access, log + reply only.

